WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
And the good guy pulling him in between the two things, and he's pressing to grind him.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
He wants to grind him, so little by little, like this.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.000
All right?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Now, David is in that position.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000
A miracle happened.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
He pushed with his legs, King David, and the whole thing,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
because the rock is on top of a pit.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
And the whole rock came down into the pit.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.000
You understand?

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
It's between two rocks, correct?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
All right?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
So the second rock is on top of what?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Of the pit.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
He pushed with his legs, and a miracle happened, and the whole thing fell down.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.000
All right?

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.000
So where is he now?

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Inside the pit.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:06.000
And that is what King David said in Tehillim.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
God, I thank you because you opened, you made wide the place where my feet were standing,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
and I was not smashed.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
It was not smashed.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.000
That day, it was Friday.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Now, what do you do Friday?

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Friday, you take a shower.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.000
You take a bath.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.000
You remember?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
How you used to take a bath?

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.000
There was no water, running water.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.000
You remember how you used to do it?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
You used to take a supple of water, or nahane, of what they used to heat up,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
and you have hot water, and somebody throws it on top of you.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Don't you remember this?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.000
They still have it for the babies.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
They put them in a little tub.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000
And they used to bring it, and they heat it up, and they put it on top of you.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
That's the way you used to do it.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.000
So now, the great general of David and Menache was Abishai.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Abishai Ben-Seduyah.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Abishai Ben-Seduyah was the great general of David.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:19.000
He had four supples, or nahane, of water, hot water, to shampoo his head.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.000
To shampoo his head with four potions of hot water.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Yes?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
All right?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Now, he saw in the water.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.000
That was like an omen of danger.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Ikeleambe, there's another version that says, no, he didn't see drops of blood.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
He saw another omen.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Atayona, he saw a bird, a pigeon, a white pigeon.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.000
It did come in.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:59.000
It was swallowed up by a hawk in front of him.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.000
He said, oh, this is as simple as what?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Something bad is happening.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
He says,

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
The Jewish people are always compared in the Torah by to a white pigeon.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Because the Israelites were compared like a pigeon in silver.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
We learn from here.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.000
He says, this must be a symbol that King David is in some sort of a trouble.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Now, Atayona Ben-Seduyah, therefore he stops taking his bath, and he goes to the house of King David.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
And he was not there.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Ammar, now, he has to go and reach King David.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.000
How is he going to find where King David is?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.000
They do it like in the movies.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.000
It doesn't make a movie.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.000
It doesn't make a movie.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.000
There's only one thing that would know where King David is.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.000
How would you find King David?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Let me, you tell me.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.000
How would you find him?

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000
You saw it before.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.000
You saw it before.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
It's going to be from the horse.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000
The horse, through the smell of the master, you would know.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.000
You're good.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.000
He cheated.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.000
He cheated.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Whose gift is it that I would wish the horse comes back?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:37.000
The horse, the only way the horse would know where King David is, only through the horse.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.000
All right?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.000
But there is a problem.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.000
There is a problem.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.000
Atayona Ben-Seduyah, he was a great general, and he was a superb politician.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
And he knows one thing.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Are you permitted to ride on the horse of the king?

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Never.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.000
You're not permitted.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Unless you want to be killed.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Unless you want to be killed.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.000
So now, Abishai was afraid.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:06.000
If I'm going to use the horse of the king, then anything goes wrong, who am I going to blame?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.000
Abishai.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.000
And if I don't save him, or I don't try to save him, whom am I going to blame?

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Abishai.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.000
Now, again, I was teaching to a class of, most of the people in my class in Bar-Ilan,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.000
they were military, and they all understood this very well.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Before you do something, then here you see the intelligence of Abishai, you check with your superior.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.000
So you know what Abishai is going to do?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.000
He's going to check with the rabbis.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Why?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
They are the experts on law.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.000
And therefore, he's going to ask the lawyers, what the lawyer said.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.000
You know what?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
He goes to the Justice Department.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Don't do things on your own.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Don't be brave.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
First, do it by the book.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.000
And that's where Abishai goes.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Amar.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.000
Tenan.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.000
The Mishnah says,

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Eyn yoshvim asuso, is forbidden to ride on the king's horse.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Eyn yoshvim akis o, you are not permitted to sit on his throne.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Vey mishtamishim besavito.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
And you are not permitted to use his staff, or scepter.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.000
Vishad asakana, now here's the rabbi.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
In a moment of danger.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Why?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Is it permitted?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.000
He goes and asks the experts on law.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.000
The law.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.000
He goes and asks the Justice Department.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.000
See?

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Justice Department.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.000
In a moment of danger, it's alright.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.000
But you see Abishai.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:37.000
He doesn't do it before he checks with the Supreme Court.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
But he cannot do it otherwise.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Because you're a general, and you have to do it through channels.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
If he knew the law, he would have done it.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
No, even if he knew the law.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Because you're not in charge of the Justice Department.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.000
He has to do it by the book.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.000
According to when?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.000
Five minutes, ten minutes, half an hour, whatever it is.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.000
But he did it by the book.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Alright, he did it by the book.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Now...

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Alright.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Then he was able to ride the king's horses.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.000
They come behind him.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000
He starts running.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.000
He was going so fast that the land seemed to be coming to him.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.000
He felt that he was not coming ahead.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.000
The land was coming.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.000
It's a beautiful feeling.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.000
You're riding a horse, and the land was coming towards him.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.000
That's right.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
It seemed like the land was running towards him.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Rushing towards him.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Alright?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.000
Now, as he was running, he was coming near that city.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.000
He sees Orpah.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.000
Orpah was the mother of Goliath and the mother of Ishmael.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Now, she was an anti-Jew.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
She could not stand a Jew.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
But what she does...

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.000
She was...

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.000
spinning.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Now, the spinning wheel in the Middle East,

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.000
if you look to your left, it looks like a sword.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.000
You see the spinning wheel?

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
That's the spinning wheel in the Middle East.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.000
Not like the spinning wheel in America,

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.000
or like in the old movies.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.000
This is the spinning wheel.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.000
So she was using a spinning wheel.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.000
She throws this on him, because he was a Jew.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.000
To kill him.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.000
She misses.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.000
Now, she tells him,

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.000
this is an old lady,

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.000
and she says,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.000
she stopped spinning,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.000
and she threw it on him.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.000
She wanted to kill him.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Now she missed.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Alam, young man,

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.000
would you return to me the...

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.000
The spinning wheel.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.000
The spinning wheel.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.000
The spinning this?

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
This?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.000
He returned to him.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.000
And it fell on her head, and she died.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
As she returned to him.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.000
He was a great general.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
Now.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.000
And she died.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.000
Now.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.000
And here in Shebi,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
when Shebi sees Abishai Ben Zeruiah,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.000
you know, coming,

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.000
Amal,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.000
Ashtabu Ben Trem,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.000
now, I could, against one,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.000
I could kill him, but two,

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
the Jews, they were very sharp,

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.000
they were like, you know, very fast.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Against two of them,

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.000
I'm not going to be able to do it.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.000
So now,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.000
Katrini, I'm afraid that both of them,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.000
they're going to kill me.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Abishai and David, they're going to kill me.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.000
You know what he did?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.000
He took David, he went down to the pit,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
and from the down there,

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.000
he threw him up.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Now comes

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Thousand and One Nights.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.000
As he was throwing him up,

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.000
he threw him up,

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
he took his spear and put it down,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.000
so that when David is going to come,

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.000
where is he going to fall?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.000
Like in the movie.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.000
Again, this is a leg,

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
this is a story, made like this

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.000
to make entertaining.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.000
To stimulate.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.000
He threw him up,

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.000
and he put his Roma,

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.000
his spear down, so that when the guy

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.000
is going to come, he's going to fall

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.000
down there.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.000
Now, Amal,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
Nipol Ala Benikta.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
Now David is going to fall, and he's going to die.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.000
Because I'm not going to fight against two of them

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.000
at the same time.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Amal Avishai Shem.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Avishai pronounces the name of God.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Of Menel David,

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.000
and David remains floating

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.000
in the air.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.000
One second, one second.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.000
I'll come to a point.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.000
And now, here it comes,

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.000
it's very important.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Penem Aleh Ivu.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.000
And why David didn't pray to God

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.000
and have him

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.000
float on the air?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
Why it depends on Avishai?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.000
En Chavush Musi Atmon

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Bet Asrin.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.000
Nobody could free himself.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.000
If you're imprisoned in a cell,

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
you cannot break away from cell

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.000
without somebody helping you from the outside.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.000
No matter how great you are,

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.000
you don't have enough Zechut to save yourself.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Somebody else could do it for you.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.000
You cannot do it sometimes for yourself.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.000
And that's something that we learned.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
David Amenet, as great as he was,

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.000
because of his own Avon, he could not implore

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.000
or invoke the name of God to protect him.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.000
He didn't do it, he didn't do it.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.000
Right, now,

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.000
Amaleh.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.000
Avishai asked him, what are you doing here?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.000
King David, you are...

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.000
God told me, what do you want?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
You want to be...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
be captive of your enemy?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
By your enemy?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Or you want your children to die?

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
And then he told him the story.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.000
And I chose to be captive rather than to live.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.000
That's why I accepted my destiny.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
All right?

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.000
This is what God told me.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.000
That's why I answered him.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
That's the deal.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Change your prayer.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.000
Change your choices, he said.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.000
Avishai said, change your choice.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.000
You made the wrong choice.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.000
The Prophet says,

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.000
let your children sell

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.000
squash

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
in the street.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.000
But you don't suffer.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Don't you suffer for your children.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.000
Let them live your life and you live your own life.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.000
That's the advice that Avishai told me,

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.000
King David.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.000
Let your children sell squash in the street

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.000
and you don't suffer for it.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.000
Let the children face it.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.000
You don't face it.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.000
I'm not there.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.000
I'm just telling you the story.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.000
I'm not there.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.000
Let them do it for themselves.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.000
That's the theory.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.000
That's right.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Well, no.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.000
To sell squash in the street means

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.000
although you have children,

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.000
but without the children you're going to work

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.000
at the lowest kind of a job,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.000
you have children, of course.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.000
You have children.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.000
So you're going to see what happens to his children.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.000
His children are going to suffer for him.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.000
Now,

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.000
let your grandson,

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.000
the son of your son,

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.000
sell squash in the street

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.000
and don't suffer

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.000
because of that.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.000
I'm not there.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
It's this prayer.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Let's pray together to God.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.000
He was a God who accepted my change.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.000
I changed my choice.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Kind of a thief.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.000
And this is what it says.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Avishai is the one who helped him.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.000
And how did he help him?

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.000
He helped him to make a prayer.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.000
To change his mind.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Then Avishai

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.000
pronounces another name of God.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.000
And David

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.000
lands in a circle.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Now they're both on ground.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.000
Between both of them

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.000
they could kill anybody.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.000
They're very sharp. They're very fast.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
They're very agile. They're very intelligent.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.000
Now, this guy,

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.000
the brother of Goliath,

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.000
was running after them.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.000
When they came to a place called Kube,

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.000
the students that I had,

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.000
they're all soldiers,

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.000
they knew what Kube was.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.000
They were explaining to me

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.000
the strategic meaning of the terrain.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.000
Let's go and attack him.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.000
Let's go and attack him.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.000
I don't know

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.000
the topography.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.000
I'm not a military man.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.000
But the students,

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.000
why they chose this place.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.000
Alright.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.000
Now they start attacking him.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.000
Then they went a little bit further down,

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
another place.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.000
Now it says,

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.000
between two little calves,

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.000
he and Avishai.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.000
Avishai and David said,

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.000
we could kill this lion.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.000
And I don't know how they attack him from both sides.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Now, when they're going to attack,

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.000
before the final killing,

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.000
you know what they're going to do to him?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.000
You know what happened, what we did today?

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.000
We killed your mother.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.000
And what happened?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.000
As soon as they told him,

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
they killed his mother, he went crazy

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.000
and they were able to kill her.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.000
That's the way they did it.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.000
Alright.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.000
He became angry.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.000
And he lost her. Then what happened?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.000
They killed her.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.000
Now, another thing.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.000
They made David

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.000
pronounce an oath, saying,

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.000
We don't want you again to go and fight.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.000
We don't want you to go. You are king.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.000
You must remain in your palace

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.000
because your security is too difficult.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.000
One minute.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
A few centuries later,

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.000
there was a woman,

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.000
a woman,

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.000
a queen.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.000
She was a gentile queen.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
She was a bad woman.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.000
She was the wife of a Jewish king.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.000
And she killed

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.000
all Ataliah.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.000
She killed all the family

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.000
of David.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Except for one person.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.000
That was the punishment.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.000
The curse came to

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.000
all his family was killed, except for one person.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.000
Except for one person.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.000
Except for one person.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.000
So then it was not equal to know.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.000
Because you know everyone was killed.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:30.000
You know also one guy

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.000
got away. And therefore,

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.000
exactly what happened to know,

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.000
it happened to David.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.000
Alright. Now, we're finished.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.000
And I just, I have ten minutes.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.000
I'm going to tell you about the golden calf.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.000
And I'm going to...

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.000
Now, before I tell you about the golden calf,

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.000
a little bit about the polar case,

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.000
it's an interesting story.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.000
Alright. And the purpose of this,

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.000
they tell you history.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.000
They teach you about human weaknesses.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:58.000
They teach you about the morality of the ethics

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.000
of respect from the leaders.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.000
And they teach you that no matter what

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.000
you do, even in a direct way,

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.000
if you are a certain stature,

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.000
you pay for it. If you don't pay it yourself,

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.000
later on to the children.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.000
Whatever happened to know,

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.000
it happened exactly to

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.000
David's king.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
Although David was the greatest,

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.000
he had to pay for it precisely because he was the greatest.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.000
Alright. It's exactly,

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.000
that's the Jewish understanding.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.000
I think it's a nice story for entertainment purposes.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Alright. Gentlemen,

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
I want to speak to you

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.000
about one of the most interesting

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.000
episodes in Jewish history.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.000
A couple of weeks ago,

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.000
we saw in the parasha how God,

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.000
himself, in person, comes,

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.000
reveals himself to the entire

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.000
people of Israel, and they shoot him.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.000
And that is, he is God, and the promise

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.000
to God, everything that you're going to tell us,

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.000
we shall do,

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.000
we shall obey.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.000
In today's parasha, Shabbat,

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.000
we're going to read about an extraordinary

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.000
case. Moses was up

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.000
in order to receive the Ten Commandments

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.000
written with the finger of God.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.000
In a minute, I'll tell you

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.000
what that means, written with the finger of God.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.000
And while God

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.000
is giving him the Ten Commandments,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.000
they build a golden camp,

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.000
they worship it,

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.000
they say, this is your God,

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.000
Israel, who took you up from evil.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.000
What happens?

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
Before this, let me explain.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.000
What does it mean that the Ten Commandments were written

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:26.000
with the finger of God?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.000
In my mind, it says like this.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.000
It doesn't use the same word as I'm using,

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.000
but this is like if you take

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.000
a microscope,

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.000
and you, I don't know,

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.000
a leaf, you see a certain pattern

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.000
in the leaf, the cells and structures

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.000
and so on,

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.000
you see that this is written by nature,

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.000
it's a natural form. In the same

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.000
way,

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.000
in the stones,

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.000
the molecules organize

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.000
that is

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.000
written,

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
so that if you see it, you see that this

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.000
is not something that was chiseled

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.000
by man,

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.000
but it was in itself, that is a miracle,

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.000
a

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.000
perennial, constant miracle,

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
that the stone itself,

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.000
just like the stones and everything has a structure

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.000
and has a pattern and so on,

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.000
in the stones themselves,

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.000
you know,

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.000
it was written, means,

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.000
in a natural way,

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.000
the Ten Commandments, you understand?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.000
So if you see the stones,

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.000
you could examine

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.000
them with a stereoscope or whatever,

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.000
it's written there,

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.000
as natural as the structure of the

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.000
own molecule.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Now, what happened,

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
what was in the mind of the Jews?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.000
Moreover,

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.000
how come that they identify

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:48.000
the state, they see the golden calf and say,

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.000
this is your God, Israel, the one who took

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.000
down the Jews?

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.000
The explanation of this

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.000
was given by the great

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.000
prophetic poet,

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Yehudah Aleinu.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.000
You just listen.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.000
That was the standard religious

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.000
practice throughout the world.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.000
Everybody believed

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.000
that the spirit of a God,

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.000
or the God, or your God,

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.000
whatever you want,

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.000
somehow takes possession

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.000
in,

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.000
not only could be in a camp,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.000
could be in something concrete.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.000
More or less, Yehudah Aleinu

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:28.000
very strongly says, since you believe that

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
the Shekhinah is in the Knis,

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.000
the Knis of theologians think of space.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.000
There's no difference between the space of a synagogue

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.000
and the space of a golden calf.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.000
You believe that the Shekhinah in the Zephyr Torah,

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
after all, Zephyr Torah is something material.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.000
The same thing, they believe

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.000
that the Shekhinah

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.000
of their God, whatever God is,

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.000
takes possession.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.000
And therefore,

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.000
this Israelites,

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:54.000
when they saw that Moses is not coming back,

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.000
they figure out, all right, let's bring

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.000
God here, and we bring God,

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.000
and he's going to be

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.000
in. This is the one that God

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.000
takes possession in the Shekhinah

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.000
of God in the golden calf,

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
and we worship it. There's nothing

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.000
wrong with it.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Now, we understand the logic

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.000
of these people.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:16.000
If this is the logic of the people,

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.000
what is the sin?

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.000
Why Moses was so angry

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:22.000
at the Jews?

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.000
Why God was so angry at the Jews?

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:26.000
And what happened?

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.000
I mean, after all, it seems logical.

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:30.000
They aren't worshipping another God.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.000
When they worshipped in the golden calf, they were thinking

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.000
that they were worshipping God.

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:36.000
What's wrong with that?

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.000
They understand the problem.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.000
Is that the Peshat? That is the Peshat.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.000
That's the Peshat.

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.000
The Peshat, they always told us

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.000
that they sinned because they were stupid.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
No.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:50.000
They say,

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.000
the Shekhinah,

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.000
see whether the Shekhinah is here

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.000
or here.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.000
Now, this is the space.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:00.000
What's the difference between this space, that's what Alevi said,

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.000
and any other space?

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.000
If the Shekhinah

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:06.000
could come to a

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:08.000
particular area, it could come to another area.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.000
What's the problem?

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:12.000
The problem basically is the following.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.000
Now you understand all about Judaism.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.000
Judaism

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:18.000
is different than all other religions

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:20.000
and the following point.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.000
Take, say,

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.000
Buddhism

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.000
or any other religion.

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.000
They worship their God in one way.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
Hope.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.000
Why do they worship God in that way?

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:34.000
Because they think

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:36.000
that this is the proper way to worship God.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:40.000
Why we worship God the way we worship God?

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.000
Not because we think

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.000
that this is the proper way.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.000
But because God explicitly

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.000
says, you do it this way.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:50.000
Now, that is the difference.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Avodah Zarah means

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.000
when man on his own

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.000
wants to determine how God

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.000
is to be worshipped.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.000
The Avon

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.000
is not because they were worshipping

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.000
another God.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.000
But because they decided

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.000
on their own to determine

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.000
how to worship God.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:14.000
If you pay attention,

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.000
and by the way, the article

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.000
in the Jewish Encyclopedia on Idolatry

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.000
is written by me. I am the author of that article.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.000
Avodah Zarah

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:24.000
doesn't mean to worship

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:26.000
a strange God.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.000
But to worship in a strange way.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.000
Avodah Shir Zarah.

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.000
Now,

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
why we say that Tefillin is good

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:38.000
and I don't know,

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.000
bowing down to Buddha is no good.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
Why not? Why not?

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.000
The difference is only one thing.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.000
Tefillin, God tells me how to do it.

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:50.000
And I'm doing it, why I'm putting

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:52.000
the Tefillin, I say it.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:54.000
Asher kideshano v'mesotave sevanu, to do this and this.

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:56.000
God has ordered me to put

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.000
the Tefillin. Why do I put the

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:00.000
Talet?

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.000
Why do I put the Talet? Because I think the Talet

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.000
is good? I say no.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.000
Asher kideshano v'mesotave sevanu.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.000
Why do I put the mezuzah outside?

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:10.000
Is it my idea to put the mezuzah?

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.000
No.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Asher kideshano v'mesotave sevanu.

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:16.000
In other words,

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.000
we worship God

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:20.000
the way He wants.

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:22.000
For men, when men wants to decide

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:24.000
how to worship God, that is idolatry.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.000
Now comes Yudan Levit,

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:28.000
something very important, very sharp.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:30.000
Therefore, if you want to be more

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.000
religious,

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:34.000
then God wants you

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.000
to be.

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:38.000
That's also Avodah Shir Zarah.

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:40.000
God wants you to do that way.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.000
You cannot be more religious than God wants you to do.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.000
Suppose I want to say, listen,

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:46.000
I want to put the Tefillin on my knee.

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.000
I want to put the Tefillin

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:50.000
in this hand and the Tefillin on that hand.

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:52.000
One minute.

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:54.000
I want to be more religious.

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:56.000
Exactly.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.000
Exactly.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:00.000
Kola mosif goreah.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.000
You cannot do it.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:04.000
Suppose I say,

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:06.000
I want to cry

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:08.000
every day for the destruction of the Bnei Meir.

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:10.000
You cannot do that.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Destruction only once a year.

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:14.000
You cannot do it.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.000
So therefore,

00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:18.000
it means, very important,

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.000
Yudan Levit says, just like

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.000
it is haram,

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:24.000
it is forbidden

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:26.000
to impose on God

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.000
something that He didn't want

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:30.000
you to do it,

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.000
so it is forbidden to add

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.000
to what God,

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:36.000
God never wanted you to do this.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:38.000
Those people.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:40.000
Only when it is too much.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:42.000
Suppose I say,

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.000
and I don't intend this,

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:46.000
that's not my purpose,

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:48.000
suppose I say, I want to worship God

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:50.000
by wearing long peyot.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:52.000
We're going to do it.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:54.000
I cannot do it the way I want it.

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:56.000
I don't have to do it.

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:58.000
I could say, I want to have peyot

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:00.000
because I like it. Fine.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.000
Fine, I want to wear it just like

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.000
that. Fine, do it.

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.000
But if you think that you're doing this for God's sake,

00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:08.000
that's not permitted.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.000
Because then you're worshiping God

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.000
according to what? To your mind.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:14.000
To your understanding.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:16.000
Yes, but

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:18.000
the major point

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
is this.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:22.000
Not only, but also the philosophy of it.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:24.000
Men cannot have the audacity

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
to tell to God, listen, I'm going now

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.000
on extra marches, now you have to give me

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:30.000
a reward for it because that's something

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.000
No. He, that's right.

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:34.000
God is the one who tells you what to do.

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.000
You will tell God, this is what you like.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.000
It's extraordinary.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
And therefore Yonah Levi says, come to the following conclusion,

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:42.000
says,

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:44.000
it's not a greater mitzvah

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.000
to cry

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:48.000
and to shabbat

00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:50.000
than to sing and shabbat

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.000
if you do it the Shem Shamayim.

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.000
Because if you cry and shabbat because of worshiping God,

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.000
He will give you as much reward

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:58.000
as when you are singing

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.000
and shabbat to rejoice God.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.000
Because it's both things you do, and why?

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:04.000
Because it's a mitzvah that God

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:06.000
rewards you.

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:08.000
I want to do it that way.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Now, of course at the time

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:12.000
he was polemicizing against the

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Karaites. The Karaites

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:16.000
in many things

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:18.000
they were more stringent than the regular Jews.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:20.000
For instance, the Karaites

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:22.000
when they used to enter into the Greece

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.000
used to remove the shoes.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:26.000
See, because they thought this is like

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:28.000
a holy place.

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:30.000
Also, they removed the shoes

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.000
before they entered into the Greece, the Karaites.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.000
Also, for instance,

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:36.000
if a woman is impure

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:38.000
and touches food,

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:40.000
we eat it, but they will not eat it.

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:42.000
They will not eat it, the Karaites, the food.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:44.000
If a woman...

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:46.000
What's the real law?

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.000
The real law is

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:50.000
God.

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:52.000
But they wanted to what?

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:54.000
To be more religious

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.000
They wanted to be more religious.

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:58.000
And God says to them, listen, this is your own

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:00.000
invention. God no place has this.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Alright?

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:04.000
And that's a very important...

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:06.000
They used to fish water. Is that haram?

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.000
The same...

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:10.000
The message is clear.

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:12.000
Anything that you do, the message

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:14.000
is clear. Anything that you do

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.000
that is not explicitly

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:18.000
demanded, if you want to

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.000
do it, listen, I like to grow a beard.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:22.000
I like, I enjoy, I look like a fine.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:24.000
But if I think, because I'm going to

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:26.000
grow a beard, or I'm going to wear

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.000
a black robe,

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:30.000
that this is more pleasant in the eyes of God,

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.000
that is wrong. That is the point that we make.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:36.000
That's a different...

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:38.000
To hand it from hand to hand.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.000
No, that's a different...

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:42.000
That's only between husband and wife.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.000
Only between husband and wife.

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:46.000
Because that's...

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:48.000
Your mother, or your sister, or your daughter

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:50.000
must be a she.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:52.000
If your wife touches the food,

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:54.000
and you don't take it directly from her hand,

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
it's not haram.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.000
But this is the point that we want to make.

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:00.000
So now, it's 7 o'clock.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.000
I don't think I have any time for the follow-up.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.000
I don't know what you're telling me.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
I have no answer. I just want to be

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:10.000
official about the follow-up case.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
Of course, you know all the incidents.

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:14.000
There are several things that bother me

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
about the follow-up case.

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:18.000
The fellow involved

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:20.000
was a Jew, regular Jew, like you and me.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
And

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
I know

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:26.000
that if we would have been approached

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:30.000
by a high officer of the

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.000
Israeli government,

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.000
and they would tell us, listen, Israel needs you.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:38.000
It's very difficult for us psychologically

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:40.000
to say no.

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:44.000
I don't know whether I would be able to say no.

00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:46.000
It's difficult.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:48.000
It's very difficult.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:52.000
And this is actually what happened with this guy Pollard.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:54.000
What happened to his wife.

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:56.000
That's why I'm a little bit

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:58.000
disappointed,

00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:00.000
disturbed.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.000
These guys, after they were used by the Israelis,

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.000
they came to the

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Israeli embassy, they knock on the door,

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:08.000
asking for

00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:10.000
asylum, and

00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:12.000
they refused.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:14.000
It bothers me.

00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:16.000
If they didn't want to give him asylum,

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:18.000
then they should not use him to begin with.

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:20.000
That's one point that I think

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:22.000
is unfair.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:26.000
I support very much UJA.

00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:30.000
Next time when we support UJA,

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.000
we should tell them, this is something that they did,

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:34.000
and you should try to amend it.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:36.000
Try to fix it, one way or the other.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:38.000
It's a young couple, they should not be

00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:40.000
condemned for life.

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:42.000
That's point number one.

00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:46.000
That's a point that nobody has made.

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:48.000
What did this guy Pollard do?

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:50.000
What he did is

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
to give some sort of information

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
to Israel

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:56.000
about the Middle East situation.

00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:58.000
This information is from America.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:00.000
America

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.000
said very correctly that we are the allies

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:04.000
of Israel.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.000
But if we are the allies of Israel,

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.000
why America

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.000
is withholding

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:12.000
this kind of information?

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:16.000
Could it be that America

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:18.000
will withhold from Israel information

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:20.000
that is so important

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.000
that could make Israel

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:24.000
win or lose a war?

00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:26.000
It seems so.

00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:28.000
And if it seems so,

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:30.000
then also

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.000
there is not only

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
what Israel did,

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.000
which is immoral, because we should not

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
spy between friends, but also what we are doing

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.000
to withhold

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:42.000
information, vital information

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:44.000
from an ally,

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.000
is as immoral

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.000
as what our ally did.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:50.000
In a sense, it could be even worse.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.000
Like the case of David and Melech with Shaul.

00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:54.000
That David and Melech made Shaul

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.000
make Avon. In a sense, also

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:58.000
America, who is our ally,

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:00.000
the ally of Israel, made Israel

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
have recourse

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.000
to have to have a spy.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.000
You understand?

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:08.000
So I see that this is a very

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.000
complex situation, and I hope

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:12.000
that one day people will know about politics.

00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:14.000
But it's important

00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:16.000
because America

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:18.000
should not withhold information,

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
vital information,

00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:22.000
from Israel. We know specifically

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.000
one single case that happened.

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:26.000
Because it's important.

00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:28.000
America, just like America in Israel's America,

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.000
we should not tolerate anybody,

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.000
especially not an ally,

00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:34.000
to spy on us.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:36.000
Also,

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:38.000
no ally should withhold

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:40.000
vital information from another ally

00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:42.000
and should not force the other

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:44.000
ally to use

00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:46.000
innocent people, like Mr. Pollard,

00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:48.000
to gain access

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:50.000
to information that should belong to them

00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:52.000
anyhow. Yes, Mickey?

00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:54.000
Because Israel told America everything that she...

00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:56.000
That everything that

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:58.000
America needs for her own

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:00.000
vital thing, of course.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.000
Of course.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.000
Whatever is vital for America,

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
Israel must do.

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:08.000
For instance, when Israel

00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:10.000
captured tanks and so on that were vital for Israel,

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:12.000
for America, immediately,

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:14.000
immediately, go to America.

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:16.000
Alright? And I believe that

00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:18.000
somebody, we should raise our...

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.000
That point should be raised

00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:22.000
among other things. That's about it.

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:24.000
And so we have next...

00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:26.000
Make an announcement

00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.000
next Monday.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:30.000
Next Monday, we're going to have the Guide to the Perplexed.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.000
You're going to enjoy it, gentlemen and ladies.

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:34.000
Alright?

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:38.000
Alright.

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:18.000
One and one.

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:20.000
It's the Gemara.

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:22.000
And I'll speak about it in a minute.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:24.000
In addition to the Gemara, we're going to speak

00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:26.000
a little bit about

00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:28.000
the Perashot Hashabua. It's one of the

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:30.000
most interesting episodes in Jewish history.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.000
The golden calf.

00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:34.000
Worshipping of the golden calf.

00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:36.000
What does it mean, exactly?

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:38.000
And, if you

00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:40.000
indulge me, I have

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.000
to say a little bit about

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:44.000
the fish elvi, as they say, about the

00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:46.000
pollock case. You know, this pie case

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
and so on.

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:50.000
Pollock, yes?

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:52.000
I want to serve you a fish elvi.

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:54.000
Alright?

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
So this is going to be the main subject.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Now, when we're starting...

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.000
Alright, go ahead.

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:04.000
Alright, go ahead.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.000
Alright.

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.000
I'll explain to you.

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:10.000
Alright.

00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:18.000
You're talking to the right...

00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:20.000
You're asking the question to the right person.

00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:22.000
I'll tell you why.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
I thought about the subject and so on.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:26.000
First of all, let me give you an extraordinary

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.000
very important fact.

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.000
Throughout

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.000
antiquity,

00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:34.000
and that's the reason why the

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Romans were so interested in

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:38.000
ancient Israel. Israel

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:40.000
was the breadbasket of the

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:42.000
Middle East. That is a fact.

00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:44.000
