00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:52.000
astrologers of

00:47:52.000 --> 00:47:54.000
Samhariv told them,

00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:56.000
if you attack today,

00:47:56.000 --> 00:47:58.000
Jerusalem.

00:47:58.000 --> 00:48:00.000
Am re'leik al da'ev.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.000
The astrologer says,

00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:04.000
if you go

00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:06.000
further

00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:08.000
today, if you advance,

00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:10.000
yachatna.

00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:12.000
Ve'ila.

00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:14.000
And if you're not going to attack it today,

00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:16.000
la yachatna.

00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:18.000
You're not going to be able to take over Jerusalem.

00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:20.000
Now,

00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:22.000
or ha derva'ah

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:24.000
lestakvoye be'atara yoma,

00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:26.000
ze'gat be'hat yoma.

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:28.000
He was so successful,

00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:30.000
yes, that a road

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.000
that normally would have taken

00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:34.000
ten days to cross for the battle,

00:48:34.000 --> 00:48:36.000
he was able to defeat

00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:38.000
everybody and he took it over

00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:40.000
in one day.

00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:42.000
He was successful. Now wait.

00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:44.000
The astrologer told him,

00:48:44.000 --> 00:48:46.000
if you advance today,

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:48.000
you're going to be able to make it.

00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:50.000
Yes. Because

00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:52.000
he was so successful,

00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:54.000
that a position or a road

00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:56.000
that would have taken ten days to take over,

00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:58.000
he was able to

00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:00.000
take it over in one day.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.000
Right?

00:49:04.000 --> 00:49:06.000
Now when they arrived by the walls,

00:49:06.000 --> 00:49:08.000
and they were actually by the walls of Jerusalem,

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:16.000
so wealthy.

00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:18.000
You know what it is?

00:49:18.000 --> 00:49:20.000
Each one threw his carpet,

00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:22.000
and out of

00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:24.000
their own carpet,

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:26.000
they make like a

00:49:26.000 --> 00:49:28.000
stair.

00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:30.000
Madre no.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.000
And he was able to climb

00:49:32.000 --> 00:49:34.000
through carpets.

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:36.000
The carpets of his officers.

00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:38.000
Thousands of officers at the end.

00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:40.000
Alright? They calculated

00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:42.000
about over a million people soldiers.

00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:44.000
It was an enormous, enormous army.

00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:46.000
One of the largest armies ever.

00:49:46.000 --> 00:49:48.000
And out of his officers'

00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:50.000
carpet,

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:52.000
each one threw,

00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:54.000
he was able to climb.

00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:56.000
Thank you.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.000
He was able to stand

00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:04.000
and see from above

00:50:04.000 --> 00:50:06.000
the walls of Jerusalem.

00:50:10.000 --> 00:50:12.000
He looked around,

00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:14.000
and was able to see underneath him

00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:16.000
all of Jerusalem.

00:50:16.000 --> 00:50:18.000
The purpose was to

00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:20.000
plan a strategy, how to attack.

00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:22.000
Thank you.

00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:24.000
As he sees it,

00:50:24.000 --> 00:50:26.000
his daughter

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:28.000
behend him,

00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:30.000
and he came down, he said,

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.000
Amad, he said to himself,

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:34.000
to everybody,

00:50:34.000 --> 00:50:36.000
Halodach ki katsadi mushnemti?

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:38.000
of Jerusalem?

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.000
Ve'alach et geshit kol meshayati?

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:42.000
That for us, I bother all my army?

00:50:42.000 --> 00:50:44.000
Did I bother to bring all my army

00:50:44.000 --> 00:50:46.000
to conquer Eric?

00:50:46.000 --> 00:50:48.000
Ve'alach kevashit

00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:50.000
kol menintah?

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.000
And because of this, I had to conquer all those

00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:54.000
other cities, to be able to reach

00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:56.000
to this unworthy spot?

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.000
It's a small thing.

00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:04.000
Ve'alachah, and it's

00:51:04.000 --> 00:51:06.000
weaker,

00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:08.000
mitkotachi avamiah,

00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:10.000
mitkof yadid,

00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:12.000
it's weaker than all the cities

00:51:12.000 --> 00:51:14.000
which I already conquered.

00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:16.000
Now,

00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:18.000
ve'alach,

00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:20.000
he goes up,

00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:22.000
ve'alach,

00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:24.000
ve'alach,

00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:26.000
that's what it says,

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:28.000
that is exactly,

00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:30.000
ve'alach,

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.000
ve'alach,

00:51:32.000 --> 00:51:34.000
ve'alach,

00:51:34.000 --> 00:51:36.000
ve'alach,

00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:38.000
ve'alach,

00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:40.000
ve'alach,

00:51:40.000 --> 00:51:42.000
ve'alach,

00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:44.000
ve'alach,

00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:46.000
he did it also when he was

00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:48.000
looking on the mountain of Zion,

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:50.000
where the Beit HaMikdash is.

00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:54.000
And when he saw the

00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:56.000
Hazara, the temple,

00:51:56.000 --> 00:51:58.000
he did the same thing.

00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:00.000
Now, of course,

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.000
when I was

00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:04.000
teaching this class,

00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:06.000
I taught it in Bar Ilan, at the University of Bar Ilan.

00:52:06.000 --> 00:52:08.000
And in my class,

00:52:08.000 --> 00:52:10.000
most of my

00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:12.000
students, I had them in the summer,

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:14.000
were

00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:16.000
military people, from the military,

00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:18.000
they come to study during the summer,

00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:20.000
most of the students at the universities

00:52:20.000 --> 00:52:22.000
are from the military, alright?

00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:24.000
So, anybody who is in the military,

00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:26.000
they understood immediately

00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:28.000
the meaning in the Gemara.

00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:30.000
The worst mistake

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.000
that any soldier could make

00:52:32.000 --> 00:52:34.000
is what?

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:36.000
When you underestimate

00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:38.000
the enemy.

00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:40.000
His mistake was, they underestimated

00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:42.000
underestimated

00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.000
they underestimated

00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:46.000
the enemy, alright?

00:52:46.000 --> 00:52:48.000
Now,

00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:50.000
Amar Lehu,

00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:52.000
Amre,

00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:54.000
Nizdeve yalaha idana,

00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:56.000
his officers are urgent.

00:52:56.000 --> 00:52:58.000
Let us attack right now.

00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:00.000
They saw Jerusalem, the Jews somehow

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.000
were unprepared,

00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:04.000
and it seemed very easy,

00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:06.000
and all the soldiers, the officers,

00:53:06.000 --> 00:53:08.000
the Sanharim, attack now!

00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:10.000
Attack now!

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:14.000
I'm surprised at you.

00:53:14.000 --> 00:53:16.000
The mahar

00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:18.000
ayatollah kol haj lihad

00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:20.000
minayku gulmo,

00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:22.000
harim minay,

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:24.000
says, all we have to do tomorrow, each one of you

00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:26.000
take a little bit of a rock

00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:28.000
from the

00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:30.000
quarter, from the wall,

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:32.000
and the whole thing collapse!

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:34.000
Why are you in such a rush?

00:53:34.000 --> 00:53:36.000
All we have to do,

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.000
you go and you take each one,

00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:40.000
take as a souvenir,

00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:42.000
because we're so many soldiers,

00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:44.000
and it seems easy,

00:53:44.000 --> 00:53:46.000
all we have to do is,

00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:48.000
each one goes, and take

00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:50.000
souvenir,

00:53:50.000 --> 00:53:52.000
alright?

00:53:52.000 --> 00:53:54.000
A souvenir.

00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:56.000
A piece of a rock as a souvenir.

00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:58.000
Yes? A pebble,

00:53:58.000 --> 00:54:00.000
from the wall.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.000
Now,

00:54:02.000 --> 00:54:04.000
a digression.

00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:06.000
I received a magazine,

00:54:06.000 --> 00:54:08.000
which is, you know,

00:54:08.000 --> 00:54:10.000
for me it's interesting,

00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:12.000
I don't know, I don't think for everybody,

00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:14.000
they tell you the latest discoveries in archaeology,

00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:16.000
it's very interesting, for me it's interesting,

00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:18.000
because I like the Bible,

00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.000
alright.

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:22.000
A couple of months ago,

00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:24.000
they had a whole issue,

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:26.000
almost the whole issue was on the Vietnamese Dutch.

00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:28.000
It's very important,

00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:30.000
because you don't understand the irony

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.000
of what's going on here.

00:54:32.000 --> 00:54:34.000
Turns out,

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:36.000
first of all, now they,

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:38.000
I should say, that the building,

00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:40.000
ever built in antiquity,

00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:42.000
and they have,

00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:44.000
now they've reconstructed from the archaeological

00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:46.000
remains, they know exactly how it looked

00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:48.000
at one time. It was 500 yards,

00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:50.000
the actual building,

00:54:50.000 --> 00:54:52.000
by 500 yards,

00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:54.000
and the height was about 130-140 yards.

00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:56.000
I'm not talking about yards,

00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:58.000
more.

00:54:58.000 --> 00:55:00.000
It was an enormous,

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.000
it was the largest building,

00:55:02.000 --> 00:55:04.000
and it was almost perfect, it was a beautiful building,

00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:06.000
but now they were able to reconstruct it.

00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:08.000
Now, in

00:55:08.000 --> 00:55:10.000
the entire

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:12.000
Vietnamese Dutch,

00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:14.000
there was absolutely zero cement, you know this?

00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:16.000
There was no cement.

00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:18.000
The stones, they were so

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:20.000
well chiseled,

00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:22.000
that they fit exactly

00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:24.000
one into the other.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:26.000
It's to perfection.

00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:28.000
Absolutely, and by the way,

00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:30.000
many of those walls are from the time of

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:32.000
Philemon Melech, because they were

00:55:32.000 --> 00:55:34.000
unable by

00:55:34.000 --> 00:55:36.000
dozens of

00:55:36.000 --> 00:55:38.000
generals that tried to attack it,

00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:40.000
but still, they stand there.

00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:42.000
By the way, they used

00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.000
also no arcs,

00:55:44.000 --> 00:55:46.000
and they don't know exactly how they were, because they had

00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:48.000
no iron beams. How they were able

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:50.000
to maintain all this without iron beams

00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:52.000
is one of the great merits. But,

00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:54.000
another thing which is telling me, some of these

00:55:54.000 --> 00:55:56.000
stones are

00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:58.000
thousands of tons

00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:00.000
in the way,

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:02.000
and they don't know exactly how they were able to

00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:04.000
take them all the way up. It's one of the great

00:56:04.000 --> 00:56:06.000
great

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:08.000
great architectural

00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:10.000
marvels of

00:56:10.000 --> 00:56:12.000
antiquity. Now, this guy

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:14.000
was so arrogant

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:18.000
that for him,

00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:20.000
when you go to Israel, you see the

00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:22.000
rocks, each one is thousands of

00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:24.000
tons. It's not like this. For him,

00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:26.000
it's like a little pebble.

00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.000
It's like a little pebble,

00:56:28.000 --> 00:56:30.000
something anybody could take.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:32.000
And this is the miracle that God

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:34.000
makes in the psychology of

00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:36.000
the enemy. Always they

00:56:36.000 --> 00:56:38.000
underestimate the Jew.

00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:40.000
Alright?

00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:42.000
Now,

00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:44.000
now,

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:46.000
the angel

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:48.000
of God came

00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:50.000
and

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:52.000
he hit

00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:54.000
and smite

00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:56.000
the

00:56:56.000 --> 00:56:58.000
army of Ashur

00:56:58.000 --> 00:57:00.000
in

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.000
185,000 of them

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:04.000
they died.

00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:06.000
Like a stream of water.

00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:08.000
They got up in the morning, the rest of the soldiers

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:10.000
were caught. Of course,

00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:12.000
we know what those angels were.

00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:14.000
Those angels were the rats

00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.000
that attacked at night

00:57:16.000 --> 00:57:18.000
and they were killed.

00:57:18.000 --> 00:57:20.000
One more verse,

00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:22.000
and then we'll finish the portion.

00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:24.000
I know the army

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:26.000
in shame, but enough.

00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:28.000
What the moment

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:30.000
passes, the opportunity

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:32.000
passes. The guy had an opportunity

00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:34.000
to destroy. He missed the opportunity

00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:36.000
and he missed it forever.

00:57:36.000 --> 00:57:38.000
Alright? Now,

00:57:38.000 --> 00:57:40.000
that's right.

00:57:40.000 --> 00:57:42.000
Now, if you have an opportunity,

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:44.000
now,

00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:46.000
here is a simple story.

00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:48.000
What's the purpose of the story?

00:57:48.000 --> 00:57:50.000
There is

00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:52.000
something that happened to us, the Jews.

00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:54.000
Alright? A great event in our history.

00:57:54.000 --> 00:57:56.000
Sam Halil comes all the way

00:57:56.000 --> 00:57:58.000
to Jerusalem.

00:57:58.000 --> 00:58:00.000
He reaches the wall

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.000
and he

00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:04.000
dies, and not he dies, his army dies

00:58:04.000 --> 00:58:06.000
and the Hachamim, a good

00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:08.000
pedigree, they make a

00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:10.000
they depict to you

00:58:10.000 --> 00:58:12.000
how Sam Halil arrived,

00:58:12.000 --> 00:58:14.000
the carpet, how he saw

00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:16.000
Jerusalem, and teaches some very important

00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:18.000
lessons. The most important lesson

00:58:18.000 --> 00:58:20.000
is what? That of an

00:58:20.000 --> 00:58:22.000
arrogant general.

00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:24.000
You know? And tells you that

00:58:24.000 --> 00:58:26.000
a great general, because of

00:58:26.000 --> 00:58:28.000
his arrogance,

00:58:28.000 --> 00:58:30.000
loses the battle.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:32.000
It's a very nice story. It teaches you a very

00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:34.000
important lesson, a very practical

00:58:34.000 --> 00:58:36.000
lesson. Alright? Don't be arrogant.

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:38.000
And you see also that, how

00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:40.000
God operates. That's right.

00:58:40.000 --> 00:58:42.000
Because the guy was, he

00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:44.000
would have been able to conquer Jerusalem.

00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:46.000
The time was right for him to conquer Jerusalem.

00:58:46.000 --> 00:58:48.000
Alright? And yet,

00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:50.000
and yet,

00:58:50.000 --> 00:58:52.000
he was arrogant.

00:58:52.000 --> 00:58:54.000
And he misjudged.

00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:56.000
Another thing that you learn from this

00:58:56.000 --> 00:58:58.000
thing, it's very very important,

00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:00.000
is that

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.000
the psychological element in war.

00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:04.000
God,

00:59:04.000 --> 00:59:06.000
first of all, Sam Halil came with all the troops

00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:08.000
and so on, but God was able to find

00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:10.000
and he saw Jerusalem as what?

00:59:10.000 --> 00:59:12.000
As something unimportant.

00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:14.000
He saw the wall as a little piece of

00:59:14.000 --> 00:59:16.000
pebble, and by

00:59:16.000 --> 00:59:18.000
underrating us,

00:59:18.000 --> 00:59:20.000
he becomes a loser. Alright?

00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:22.000
Now, we're going to continue

00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:24.000
with another story.

00:59:24.000 --> 00:59:26.000
This story is the

00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:28.000
closest that we have to a thousand and one.

00:59:28.000 --> 00:59:30.000
When you were a child,

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:32.000
sometimes you heard the stories of a thousand and one

00:59:32.000 --> 00:59:34.000
nights. Here, you're going to have

00:59:34.000 --> 00:59:36.000
a story, which is written

00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:38.000
for the popular message,

00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:40.000
for entertainment.

00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:42.000
It's going to be like a magical, like a thousand and one

00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:44.000
night, like El Tilele Ulele, alright?

00:59:44.000 --> 00:59:46.000
But it has a moral to it.

00:59:46.000 --> 00:59:48.000
And it's to

00:59:48.000 --> 00:59:50.000
this extraordinary combination,

00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:52.000
only in the Talmud you find it.

00:59:52.000 --> 00:59:54.000
To combine great entertainment

00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:56.000
for the masses,

00:59:56.000 --> 00:59:58.000
and at the same time, what?

00:59:58.000 --> 01:00:00.000
First-rate education.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.000
Like we had just now, entertainment education.

01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:04.000
But here, what the story that we're going to study now

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:06.000
is a story of

01:00:06.000 --> 01:00:08.000
pure entertainment. I heard it

01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:10.000
when I was a little child. My grandfather and I

01:00:10.000 --> 01:00:12.000
have heard this story, and I'm sure,

01:00:12.000 --> 01:00:14.000
or maybe some of you may remember this story

01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:16.000
from your parents or your grandparents.

01:00:16.000 --> 01:00:18.000
It's a great, nice story.

01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:20.000
Alright? For children, they love it.

01:00:20.000 --> 01:00:22.000
Now,

01:00:22.000 --> 01:00:24.000
this story is like this.

01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:26.000
Tishbi

01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:28.000
was the brother of Goliath.

01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:30.000
Goliath, you remember the famous

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:32.000
giant?

01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:34.000
Goliath, who fought with David

01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:36.000
and David defeated him, alright?

01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:38.000
Now,

01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:40.000
Goliath had a brother,

01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:42.000
and his brother was

01:00:42.000 --> 01:00:44.000
Tishbi, alright?

01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:46.000
Tishbi, Beno.

01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:48.000
He was living,

01:00:48.000 --> 01:00:50.000
dwelling in the city of Noah.

01:00:50.000 --> 01:00:52.000
Asher

01:00:52.000 --> 01:00:54.000
bidideh harafa.

01:00:54.000 --> 01:00:56.000
And here I was,

01:00:56.000 --> 01:00:58.000
there I was with the Repaim.

01:00:58.000 --> 01:01:00.000
The Repaim of ethical

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.000
people, called Repaim.

01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:04.000
Who were

01:01:04.000 --> 01:01:06.000
giants. By giants,

01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:08.000
we mean like we have giants in Africa.

01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:10.000
Maybe they were eight feet, or

01:01:10.000 --> 01:01:12.000
seven feet tall, very, very

01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:14.000
tall. This was documented, by the

01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:16.000
way, because we know from the bones and other things

01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:18.000
that there were actually people

01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:20.000
like, like we know, like you have the

01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:22.000
Watusi tribes in Africa and so

01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:24.000
on, that were very, very tall,

01:01:24.000 --> 01:01:26.000
very, very big, and in Israel

01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:28.000
there was a group of people,

01:01:28.000 --> 01:01:30.000
yes, a tribe, a small

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:32.000
tribe of pagans,

01:01:32.000 --> 01:01:34.000
called the Repaim.

01:01:34.000 --> 01:01:36.000
And Goliath

01:01:36.000 --> 01:01:38.000
was from this group

01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:40.000
of Repaim.

01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:42.000
These were giants. By giants, we mean

01:01:42.000 --> 01:01:44.000
that doesn't have to be

01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:46.000
ten yards tall.

01:01:46.000 --> 01:01:48.000
But these were, were seven, eight

01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:50.000
feet tall. They were like the Watusi

01:01:50.000 --> 01:01:52.000
tribe, alright? They were very, very big.

01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:54.000
And this Tishbi

01:01:54.000 --> 01:01:56.000
was with a group of

01:01:56.000 --> 01:01:58.000
an ankle of this

01:01:58.000 --> 01:02:00.000
size, the Repaim head, by the

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.000
stature of Noah.

01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:04.000
And the weight

01:02:04.000 --> 01:02:06.000
of his armor,

01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:08.000
he used to wear an armor,

01:02:10.000 --> 01:02:12.000
300

01:02:12.000 --> 01:02:14.000
ounces,

01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:16.000
or something, I don't know.

01:02:16.000 --> 01:02:18.000
It was very, very heavy, alright?

01:02:18.000 --> 01:02:20.000
Very heavy.

01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:22.000
Yes.

01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:24.000
And he had

01:02:24.000 --> 01:02:26.000
just made a new sword for

01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:28.000
a young man.

01:02:28.000 --> 01:02:30.000
And he said,

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:32.000
I am going to

01:02:32.000 --> 01:02:34.000
take revenge

01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:36.000
on David because

01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:38.000
he killed his brother.

01:02:38.000 --> 01:02:40.000
He wanted to get his revenge.

01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:42.000
Alright? Now,

01:02:42.000 --> 01:02:44.000
might the Tishbi

01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:46.000
have to say that this

01:02:46.000 --> 01:02:48.000
Mr. Tishbi

01:02:48.000 --> 01:02:50.000
was dwelling or living

01:02:50.000 --> 01:02:52.000
by Noah. What's the relation?

01:02:52.000 --> 01:02:54.000
Tishbi

01:02:54.000 --> 01:02:56.000
and Noah. So you have to

01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:58.000
underline that.

01:02:58.000 --> 01:03:00.000
I'm not arguing.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.000
Tishbi

01:03:02.000 --> 01:03:04.000
and Noah.

01:03:04.000 --> 01:03:06.000
King Saul

01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:08.000
was jealous of David.

01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:10.000
David was the son-in-law.

01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:12.000
David had married

01:03:12.000 --> 01:03:14.000
Michal, the daughter of Saul.

01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:16.000
And Saul was very, very

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:18.000
jealous. He wanted to get rid of her.

01:03:18.000 --> 01:03:20.000
Finally,

01:03:20.000 --> 01:03:22.000
when the

01:03:22.000 --> 01:03:24.000
father-in-law wants to kill him, he runs.

01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:28.000
And they had

01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:30.000
the Urim Betumim.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.000
They had the famous stones.

01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:34.000
And they would give you an answer.

01:03:34.000 --> 01:03:36.000
Now,

01:03:36.000 --> 01:03:38.000
there were a few people with David.

01:03:38.000 --> 01:03:40.000
David was in the desert and they were

01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:42.000
starving to death. They had no food.

01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:44.000
They went to the city of

01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.000
Noah and he says,

01:03:46.000 --> 01:03:48.000
Go ahead,

01:03:48.000 --> 01:03:50.000
give me some food and give me

01:03:50.000 --> 01:03:52.000
weapons.

01:03:52.000 --> 01:03:54.000
The people in Noah, they didn't know that Saul

01:03:54.000 --> 01:03:56.000
wanted to kill him. There was no telegraph.

01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:58.000
No television.

01:03:58.000 --> 01:04:00.000
So the guardian says,

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.000
What happened?

01:04:02.000 --> 01:04:04.000
And David,

01:04:04.000 --> 01:04:06.000
I'm in a secret mission. I'm alone.

01:04:06.000 --> 01:04:08.000
I have a few people waiting for me outside.

01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:10.000
I need a weapon and I need

01:04:10.000 --> 01:04:12.000
food.

01:04:12.000 --> 01:04:14.000
To make the story short,

01:04:14.000 --> 01:04:16.000
they give him a weapon. The weapon

01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:18.000
that they give him is the sword of Goliath.

01:04:18.000 --> 01:04:20.000
That once he had used to kill.

01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.000
Do you remember when he killed Goliath? He killed him with his own sword.

01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:24.000
Do you remember the story?

01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:26.000
That sword was kept in Noah.

01:04:26.000 --> 01:04:28.000
The Kohanim kept the sword.

01:04:28.000 --> 01:04:30.000
He goes.

01:04:32.000 --> 01:04:34.000
When Saul finds out

01:04:34.000 --> 01:04:36.000
that this

01:04:36.000 --> 01:04:38.000
is what happened. He comes there

01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:40.000
and he kills the entire

01:04:40.000 --> 01:04:42.000
city of Kohanim

01:04:42.000 --> 01:04:44.000
except for one.

01:04:44.000 --> 01:04:46.000
One person is left.

01:04:46.000 --> 01:04:48.000
Now

01:04:48.000 --> 01:04:50.000
God is going to

01:04:50.000 --> 01:04:52.000
punish

01:04:52.000 --> 01:04:54.000
because of the

01:04:54.000 --> 01:04:56.000
abomination of Noah.

01:04:56.000 --> 01:04:58.000
Who

01:04:58.000 --> 01:05:00.000
in your mind?

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.000
Saul.

01:05:02.000 --> 01:05:04.000
He lied.

01:05:04.000 --> 01:05:06.000
Saul.

01:05:06.000 --> 01:05:08.000
He killed everybody.

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:10.000
The whole city. The people were innocent.

01:05:10.000 --> 01:05:12.000
They were Kohanim.

01:05:12.000 --> 01:05:14.000
That makes sense.

01:05:14.000 --> 01:05:16.000
David. Now the one who is going to be punished is David.

01:05:16.000 --> 01:05:18.000
Why?

01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:20.000
He caused it.

01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:22.000
He shouldn't have gone there. He has his own problem

01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.000
with his father-in-law.

01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:26.000
He shouldn't have involved other innocent people

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:28.000
in the stream.

01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:30.000
Therefore, you see,

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.000
normally we think the one who is going to be punished

01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:34.000
is Saul. Of course Saul is going to be punished.

01:05:34.000 --> 01:05:36.000
But the one that is going to make the hallowed balloon

01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:38.000
is not going to be Saul.

01:05:38.000 --> 01:05:40.000
The hallowed balloon is going to be

01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:42.000
David.

01:05:42.000 --> 01:05:44.000
Because David, he is

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.000
in a sense deceiving

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:48.000
and implicating other people.

01:05:48.000 --> 01:05:50.000
I thought they were innocent. They didn't know anything about it.

01:05:50.000 --> 01:05:52.000
They didn't know about this.

01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:54.000
In a sense

01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:56.000
because he caused. Now,

01:05:56.000 --> 01:05:58.000
here you see something very important.

01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:00.000
If I am a good guy

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.000
and I cause somebody

01:06:02.000 --> 01:06:04.000
provoking somebody to punch me in the nose,

01:06:06.000 --> 01:06:08.000
I as a rabbi,

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:10.000
I am responsible

01:06:10.000 --> 01:06:12.000
for what this guy punched me in the nose.

01:06:12.000 --> 01:06:14.000
I should not make him punch me in the nose.

01:06:14.000 --> 01:06:16.000
In other words, I should not provoke him.

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:18.000
In other words, here David,

01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:20.000
because he is held in a higher standard,

01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:22.000
he is not like a common person.

01:06:22.000 --> 01:06:24.000
So, by provoking

01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:26.000
Saul,

01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:28.000
David is responsible.

01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:30.000
In other words, if I am a rabbi,

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:32.000
or I am a great individual,

01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:34.000
like David Amed, and I make somebody

01:06:34.000 --> 01:06:36.000
curse me,

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:38.000
hit me,

01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:40.000
spit on my face,

01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:42.000
I don't know, do something bad.

01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:44.000
I am responsible.

01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:46.000
I should not have made him do that.

01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:50.000
Alright? You can't cause somebody

01:06:50.000 --> 01:06:52.000
and here we are going to see

01:06:52.000 --> 01:06:54.000
the subtlety of the Gemara.

01:06:54.000 --> 01:06:56.000
What happened there was nothing.

01:06:56.000 --> 01:06:58.000
It is going to be told, as I say,

01:06:58.000 --> 01:07:00.000
as a fairy tale,

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:02.000
but the story is not.

01:07:02.000 --> 01:07:04.000
It is like a fairy tale for children.

01:07:05.000 --> 01:07:07.000
But he should have.

01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:09.000
He is smarter. He is greater.

01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:11.000
In other words,

01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:13.000
here you see the irony of this.

01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.000
Because David was greater

01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:17.000
than Saul Amed,

01:07:17.000 --> 01:07:19.000
of course,

01:07:19.000 --> 01:07:21.000
and the guy is gone. Don't worry.

01:07:21.000 --> 01:07:23.000
At the end, you know what happened?

01:07:23.000 --> 01:07:25.000
Saul and all his children died.

01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:27.000
That is bad. Alright?

01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:29.000
But David,

01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:31.000
he also has to pay

01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:33.000
for his mistakes.

01:07:33.000 --> 01:07:35.000
Maybe he didn't anticipate

01:07:35.000 --> 01:07:37.000
that Saul would be so wicked.

01:07:37.000 --> 01:07:39.000
It makes no difference.

01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:41.000
David is not like us.

01:07:41.000 --> 01:07:43.000
David,

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:45.000
he should not have

01:07:45.000 --> 01:07:47.000
even taken a risk,

01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:49.000
one in a thousand,

01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:51.000
to sacrifice or to risk

01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:53.000
this innocent Kohanim

01:07:53.000 --> 01:07:55.000
in the middle of nowhere.

01:07:55.000 --> 01:07:57.000
You come, you are the son and daughter of the king.

01:07:57.000 --> 01:07:59.000
You say, I am on a secret mission.

01:07:59.000 --> 01:08:01.000
They are going to believe you.

01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:03.000
You see?

01:08:03.000 --> 01:08:05.000
So, on account of this,

01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:07.000
David is going to

01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:09.000
pay for it.

01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:13.000
Yeah.

01:08:13.000 --> 01:08:15.000
Maybe they would not have given bread

01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:17.000
because they would not be able to get into...

01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:19.000
But that would be their choice.

01:08:19.000 --> 01:08:21.000
Alright?

01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:23.000
But he should not have lied to them.

01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:25.000
Their choice.

01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:27.000
If their choice is, well, we want to take a risk,

01:08:27.000 --> 01:08:29.000
alright, that's your choice.

01:08:29.000 --> 01:08:31.000
Alright?

01:08:31.000 --> 01:08:33.000
And on top of that, they gave him a weapon.

01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:35.000
They were giving him the sword of Goliath.

01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:37.000
So it means that they are arming him

01:08:37.000 --> 01:08:39.000
to fight against his father-in-law.

01:08:39.000 --> 01:08:41.000
And then Saul

01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:43.000
got raided mad

01:08:43.000 --> 01:08:45.000
and just wiped out the whole city.

01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:47.000
Except for one, alright?

01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:49.000
Now,

01:08:49.000 --> 01:08:51.000
Amar Rabi Ulam Arab

01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:53.000
ishe v'al etkinol.

01:08:53.000 --> 01:08:55.000
This ishbi.

01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:57.000
You know why he wanted to kill David?

01:08:57.000 --> 01:08:59.000
Because he, in his mind,

01:08:59.000 --> 01:09:01.000
was because he killed his brother Goliath.

01:09:01.000 --> 01:09:03.000
But actually, God put this in his mind

01:09:03.000 --> 01:09:05.000
to make David

01:09:05.000 --> 01:09:07.000
pay

01:09:07.000 --> 01:09:09.000
for the sin that he caused

01:09:09.000 --> 01:09:11.000
in the city of Noah.

01:09:11.000 --> 01:09:13.000
In other words,

01:09:13.000 --> 01:09:15.000
if some jahish comes to attack us,

01:09:15.000 --> 01:09:17.000
sometimes it's not the jahish himself,

01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:19.000
it's that maybe we did

01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:21.000
something

01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:23.000
that God is sending

01:09:23.000 --> 01:09:25.000
using this jahish

01:09:25.000 --> 01:09:27.000
Mr., I don't know,

01:09:27.000 --> 01:09:29.000
T.

01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:33.000
Mr. T.

01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:35.000
Mr. T comes and attacks us.

01:09:35.000 --> 01:09:37.000
This is because God

01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:39.000
sometimes

01:09:39.000 --> 01:09:41.000
puts an idea in his hand,

01:09:41.000 --> 01:09:43.000
and that's what happened.

01:09:43.000 --> 01:09:45.000
This ishbi was from the Rephaim,

01:09:45.000 --> 01:09:47.000
the giant, alright?

01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:49.000
Mr. Giant, and

01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:51.000
what's the name of this guy, a wrestler?

01:09:51.000 --> 01:09:53.000
Mr. Hulk.

01:09:53.000 --> 01:09:55.000
Hulk Hogan.

01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:57.000
This guy comes,

01:09:57.000 --> 01:09:59.000
and he wants to make this guy a little bit bigger.

01:09:59.000 --> 01:10:01.000
And David Amelek was a normal size.

01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:03.000
Alright?

01:10:03.000 --> 01:10:05.000
So, this guy, it was

01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:07.000
God sending him against

01:10:07.000 --> 01:10:09.000
Amman Rehka,

01:10:09.000 --> 01:10:11.000
who I call David.

01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:13.000
God says to David, since you're such a good guy,

01:10:13.000 --> 01:10:15.000
I'm going to give you a choice.

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:17.000
He says, I'm not telling you I won't dare

01:10:17.000 --> 01:10:19.000
to move your car.

01:10:19.000 --> 01:10:21.000
How long can you keep this sin

01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:23.000
hidden in your hand?

01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:25.000
In other words,

01:10:25.000 --> 01:10:27.000
this sin, nobody suspected of it.

01:10:27.000 --> 01:10:29.000
You have hidden it.

01:10:29.000 --> 01:10:31.000
Because everybody thinks

01:10:31.000 --> 01:10:33.000
that you're innocent,

01:10:33.000 --> 01:10:35.000
that the only one who is guilty

01:10:35.000 --> 01:10:37.000
is Shaul.

01:10:37.000 --> 01:10:39.000
You are hidding the sin.

01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:41.000
How long are you going to keep it hidden?

01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:43.000
I'm going to punish you,

01:10:43.000 --> 01:10:45.000
as he said.

01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:47.000
And Rehka, because of you,

01:10:47.000 --> 01:10:49.000
was killed because of you.

01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:53.000
The whole city of Koranim

01:10:53.000 --> 01:10:55.000
was killed because of you.

01:10:59.000 --> 01:11:01.000
Very important.

01:11:01.000 --> 01:11:03.000
Who was the general who carried on the order

01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:05.000
of Shaul?

01:11:05.000 --> 01:11:07.000
Doeg HaAlamin.

01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:09.000
This Doeg HaAlamin,

01:11:09.000 --> 01:11:11.000
he lost his word to come.

01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:13.000
Why did he come?

01:11:13.000 --> 01:11:15.000
Because he obeyed the order of Shaul.

01:11:15.000 --> 01:11:17.000
But who was responsible?

01:11:17.000 --> 01:11:19.000
It was responsible David.

01:11:19.000 --> 01:11:21.000
David, you are responsible

01:11:21.000 --> 01:11:23.000
for the people

01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:25.000
that were killed

01:11:25.000 --> 01:11:27.000
and also for the people who killed.

01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:29.000
The killers became killers

01:11:29.000 --> 01:11:31.000
because of you, David.

01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:33.000
Not only are you responsible for those

01:11:33.000 --> 01:11:35.000
who were murdered,

01:11:35.000 --> 01:11:37.000
but for those who became murderers.

01:11:41.000 --> 01:11:43.000
You are responsible for those

01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:45.000
who were murdered

01:11:45.000 --> 01:11:47.000
and for those who became murderers.

01:11:51.000 --> 01:11:53.000
And because of you,

01:11:53.000 --> 01:11:55.000
eventually Shaul was punished.

01:11:55.000 --> 01:11:57.000
And his three children

01:11:57.000 --> 01:11:59.000
that they died in the war in Palestine,

01:11:59.000 --> 01:12:01.000
they died why?

01:12:01.000 --> 01:12:03.000
To pay for the Avon that they make in Nome.

01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:05.000
And who caused the Avon?

01:12:05.000 --> 01:12:07.000
Destiny.

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:09.000
You see that the level of morality

01:12:09.000 --> 01:12:11.000
that we have,

01:12:11.000 --> 01:12:13.000
the higher you are,

01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:17.000
the higher standard that the Torah demands of you.

01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:21.000
And we all think that

01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:23.000
David, you are responsible for those who became murderers.

01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:27.000
You are responsible, Mr. David.

01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:29.000
And truly, David

01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:31.000
was the great

01:12:31.000 --> 01:12:33.000
symbol of Jewish

01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:35.000
piety and so on, and therefore

01:12:35.000 --> 01:12:37.000
he held it.

01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:39.000
No, no.

01:12:39.000 --> 01:12:41.000
But David

01:12:41.000 --> 01:12:43.000
because of his mother God,

01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:45.000
he is held responsible.

01:12:45.000 --> 01:12:47.000
Now, he says,

01:12:47.000 --> 01:12:49.000
you have a choice.

01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:53.000
Either your children shall be exterminated

01:12:55.000 --> 01:12:57.000
You make a choice.

01:12:57.000 --> 01:12:59.000
I have to punish you, that's it.

01:13:03.000 --> 01:13:05.000
Or you're going to be

01:13:05.000 --> 01:13:07.000
caught by one of your enemies.

01:13:07.000 --> 01:13:09.000
What do you prefer?

01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:11.000
To have your children exterminated,

01:13:11.000 --> 01:13:13.000
David,

01:13:13.000 --> 01:13:15.000
or you to fall

01:13:15.000 --> 01:13:17.000
captive

01:13:17.000 --> 01:13:19.000
by one of your enemies,

01:13:19.000 --> 01:13:21.000
to one of your enemies to capture you.

01:13:21.000 --> 01:13:23.000
What do you prefer?

01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:25.000
This is a choice.

01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:27.000
I prefer to fall

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:29.000
captured

01:13:29.000 --> 01:13:31.000
to be captured by one of my enemies.

01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:33.000
Now,

01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:35.000
you're going to be captured today.

01:13:35.000 --> 01:13:37.000
I remember as a child

01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:39.000
how my grandfather used to tell me this story.

01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:43.000
You see, I grew

01:13:43.000 --> 01:13:45.000
when I was

01:13:45.000 --> 01:13:47.000
20, 30 years old.

01:13:47.000 --> 01:13:49.000
I grew up

01:13:49.000 --> 01:13:51.000
in a village

01:13:51.000 --> 01:13:53.000
in a small village

01:13:53.000 --> 01:13:55.000
and I was

01:13:55.000 --> 01:13:57.000
20, 30 years behind

01:13:57.000 --> 01:13:59.000
American technology.

01:13:59.000 --> 01:14:01.000
In my day, there was no

01:14:01.000 --> 01:14:03.000
television,

01:14:03.000 --> 01:14:05.000
even radio was, but the radio

01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:07.000
was in Spanish.

01:14:07.000 --> 01:14:09.000
No cars, no nothing.

01:14:09.000 --> 01:14:11.000
So what we had, our grandparents

01:14:11.000 --> 01:14:13.000
used to tell us stories.

01:14:13.000 --> 01:14:15.000
So I grew up in a time

01:14:15.000 --> 01:14:17.000
where the only entertainment

01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:21.000
I remember,

01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:23.000
was a time there was no radio, no television,

01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:25.000
no nothing. That's it.

01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:27.000
Now,

01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:29.000
now one day,

01:14:29.000 --> 01:14:31.000
yes,

01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:33.000
Yamaha in a Turkish car

01:14:33.000 --> 01:14:35.000
was dying. He went for hunting.

01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:37.000
That was the best.

01:14:37.000 --> 01:14:39.000
Go hunting, go hunting.

01:14:39.000 --> 01:14:41.000
Go hunting.

01:14:41.000 --> 01:14:43.000
King Satan,

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:45.000
Satan the devil,

01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:47.000
disappeared like a beautiful deer.

01:14:47.000 --> 01:14:49.000
A beautiful deer.

01:14:49.000 --> 01:14:51.000
And there was a great

01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:53.000
marksman, David.

01:14:53.000 --> 01:14:55.000
He

01:14:55.000 --> 01:14:57.000
with a bow and arrow,

01:14:57.000 --> 01:14:59.000
and he aimed at the deer.

01:14:59.000 --> 01:15:01.000
And,

01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:03.000
he threw the arrow.

01:15:07.000 --> 01:15:09.000
Now, what happened?

01:15:09.000 --> 01:15:11.000
Every time he would be following the deer.

01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:13.000
So another

01:15:13.000 --> 01:15:15.000
aimed at the deer,

01:15:15.000 --> 01:15:17.000
and he throws the arrow.

01:15:17.000 --> 01:15:19.000
Pulling him,

01:15:19.000 --> 01:15:21.000
throwing him where?

01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:23.000
Into the north territory.

01:15:23.000 --> 01:15:25.000
Into that enclave where the

01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:27.000
giants are there.

01:15:27.000 --> 01:15:29.000
In other words, he is being

01:15:29.000 --> 01:15:31.000
hunted

01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:33.000
by the deer.

01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:35.000
Normally you hunt the deer.

01:15:35.000 --> 01:15:37.000
This time the deer was hunting him.

01:15:37.000 --> 01:15:39.000
What?

01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:41.000
That's right.

01:15:41.000 --> 01:15:43.000
And the deer was moving,

01:15:43.000 --> 01:15:45.000
and David became so engrossed

01:15:45.000 --> 01:15:47.000
that every time he would aim,

01:15:47.000 --> 01:15:49.000
misses.

01:15:49.000 --> 01:15:51.000
And he misses, and the deer runs out of it.

01:15:51.000 --> 01:15:53.000
So you follow the deer.

01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:55.000
He's not thinking,

01:15:55.000 --> 01:15:57.000
he's engrossed in the hunting.

01:15:57.000 --> 01:15:59.000
He doesn't know that this is

01:15:59.000 --> 01:16:01.000
in order to pay for the harm that he did

01:16:01.000 --> 01:16:03.000
with

01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:05.000
Noah.

01:16:05.000 --> 01:16:07.000
Now,

01:16:07.000 --> 01:16:09.000
until

01:16:09.000 --> 01:16:11.000
he came

01:16:11.000 --> 01:16:13.000
into Palestine,

01:16:13.000 --> 01:16:15.000
the Palestinian territory.

01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:17.000
That was the Palestinians.

01:16:17.000 --> 01:16:19.000
Right?

01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:21.000
The Palestinians.

01:16:21.000 --> 01:16:23.000
Now,

01:16:23.000 --> 01:16:25.000
when

01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:27.000
Eshvi saw him from Noah,

01:16:27.000 --> 01:16:29.000
saw who?

01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:31.000
David.

01:16:31.000 --> 01:16:33.000
This is the guy

01:16:33.000 --> 01:16:35.000
who murdered

01:16:35.000 --> 01:16:37.000
my brother Goliath.

01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:39.000
Murdered

01:16:39.000 --> 01:16:41.000
him.

01:16:41.000 --> 01:16:43.000
Now, he wanted

01:16:43.000 --> 01:16:45.000
to really take revenge.

01:16:45.000 --> 01:16:47.000
Now comes the south.

01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:53.000
There was, and this is true,

01:16:53.000 --> 01:16:55.000
you see Goliath, there is

01:16:55.000 --> 01:16:57.000
many oil presses.

01:16:57.000 --> 01:16:59.000
To press oil.

01:16:59.000 --> 01:17:01.000
For oil.

01:17:01.000 --> 01:17:03.000
You know how you press oil?

01:17:03.000 --> 01:17:05.000
You have like a big pit.

01:17:05.000 --> 01:17:07.000
And on top of the pit

01:17:07.000 --> 01:17:09.000
there is a rock.

01:17:09.000 --> 01:17:11.000
And on top of the rock

01:17:11.000 --> 01:17:13.000
there is another rock.

